---Base type common to all user interface elements. The following components inherit from this:
---
---Handling Events: Components can set as listeners for certain events, allowing developers to trigger actions in
---response. These range from events triggered on that component, such as mouse clicks, to global events, such as
---variable transmissions.
---
---State Properties: The following properties relate to how the user interacts with the component and how the component
---reacts to said interactions.
---
---Restricted Components: In some cases, components may be flagged as restricted, preventing certain operations from
---working from the Lua-side, or resulting in them yielding default values instead.
---
---Components can be intentionally tagged as restricted through the `Component:FlagRestricted()` function, with the
---restricted status being verifiable via `component.isRestricted`.
---
---Warning: Once restricted, a component cannot become unrestricted afterwards.
---
---Warning: Flagging a component as restricted is only possible if the current plugin is its creator.
---@class ui.Component
---@field position ui.Pos Gets or sets this component's origin.
---@field size ui.Size Gets or sets the dimensions for this component.
---@field isSafeAreaRelative boolean Whether or not layout operations involving this component take into account the device's safe areas.
---@field x integer (Read-only) Current horizontal position for this component relative to its parent.
---@field y integer (Read-only) Current vertical position for this component relative to its parent.
---@field width integer (Read-only) Current width for this component.
---@field height integer (Read-only) Current height for this component.
---@field xyLocal Vector2 (Read-only) Current XY position for this component relative to its parent.
---@field xyGlobal Vector2 (Read-only) Current absolute XY position for this component.
---@field alpha number Controls how opaque this component appears, ranges from 0 (fully transparent) to 1 (opaque).
---@field rgb integer Hexadecimal colour code representing the Red, Green, and Blue tints for this component.
---@field rgba integer Hexadecimal colour code representing the Red, Green, Blue, And Alpha tints for this component.
---@field colour Vector4 Red, Green, Blue, and Alpha tints represented as a 4-channel vector, with each channel limited to a 0..1 range. On assignment, values outside of this range will be clamped.
---@field hidden boolean Controls whether this component is visible. This only applies to Lua-side visibility, and cannot be used to force built-in UI components to become visible.
---@field visible boolean (Read-only) Indicates whether this component is visible or not. This state refers only to the internal state of this component. For the global visibility state see `visibleGlobal`. Differs from `hidden` in that this also takes into account built-in UI component visibility.
---@field visibleGlobal boolean (Read-only) Indicates whether this component is visible within the UI component tree. For example, will return `false` if any parent of this component is not visible.
---@field stylesheetID integer ID for the StyleSheet currently in use by this component, or -1 if no StyleSheet is active.
---@field aspectRatioProportion number (Read-only) The aspect ratio width value divided by the height value. For example, a `16:10` ratio resolves to a proportion of `1.6`.
---@field aspectRatioWidth integer (Read-only) The target width value used for aspect ratio calculations. Note this value is always `1` or higher, even when aspect ratio scaling is disabled.
---@field aspectRatioHeight integer (Read-only) The target height value used for aspect ratio calculations. Note this value is always `1` or higher, even when aspect ratio scaling is disabled.
---@field aspectRatioMode ui.AspectRatioMode (Read-only) Mode used when determining how the aspect ratio should be applied to this component, if at all.
---@field enabled boolean Controls whether this component responds to inputs and events.
---@field clickthrough boolean Controls whether mouse interactions on this component block interactions on components below it.
---@field isMouseOver boolean (Read-only) Whether the cursor is currently over this component or not.
---@field isClicked boolean (Read-only) Whether the user has clicked on this component recently or not.
---@field opConfig ui.ComponentOpConfig Identifies the action to perform when the component is interacted with.
---@field dragConfig ui.ComponentDragConfig Determines how the component reacts to drag actions.
---@field swipeConfig ui.ComponentSwipeConfig Determines how the component reacts to swipe gestures.
---@field pinchConfig ui.ComponentPinchConfig Determines how the component reacts to pinch gestures.
---@field cursorConfig ui.ComponentCursorConfig Specifies which cursors to use, if any, when interacting with this component.
---@field paramsConfig ui.ComponentParamsConfig Additional parameters attached to this component.
---@field type ui.ComponentType (Read-only) ID identifying the type of this component.
---@field parent ui.Component? (Read-only) The immediate parent of this component within the UI component tree. Returns `nil` if there is no parent.
---@field parentStatic ui.Component? (Read-only) The static parent of this component within the UI component tree. Returns `nil` if there is no static parent.
---@field parentInterface ui.Interface (Read-only) Interface in which this component resides.
---@field interfaceID integer (Read-only) ID identifying the interface in which this component resides.
---@field staticID integer (Read-only) ID identifying the static component on which this component resides.
---@field categoryID integer (Read-only) ID identifying the dynamic ID category this component's using, or -1 if this is a static component.
---@field dynamicID integer (Read-only) ID identifying the dynamic ID category this component's using, or -1 if this is a static component.
local Component = {}

---Moves this component's origin to the provided coordinates, optionally taking into account the parent's dimensions,
---and this component's own dimensions.
---
---Info: `SetPos` should be preferred over using SetX and SetY separately as it involves less layout operations.
---@param x integer Absolute horizontal coordinate to move this component to in interface units
---@param parentPercentageX? number If specified, offsets this component's horizontal origin based on a percentage of its parent's width.
---@param selfPercentageX? number If specified, offsets this component's horizontal origin based on a percentage of its width.
function Component:SetX(x, parentPercentageX, selfPercentageX) end

---Moves this component's origin to the provided coordinates, optionally taking into account the parent's dimensions,
---and this component's own dimensions.
---
---Info: `SetPos` should be preferred over using SetX and SetY separately as it involves less layout operations.
---@param y integer Absolute vertical coordinate to move this component to in interface units
---@param parentPercentageY? number If specified, offsets this component's vertical origin based on a percentage of its parent's height.
---@param selfPercentageY? number If specified, offsets this component's vertical origin based on a percentage of its height.
function Component:SetY(y, parentPercentageY, selfPercentageY) end

---Moves this component's origin to the provided coordinates, optionally taking into account the parent's dimensions,
---and this component's own dimensions.
---
---Info: `SetPos` should be preferred over using SetX and SetY separately as it involves less layout operations.
---
---In the client: In one check, the self percentages moved a component the opposite way to this description: SetPos(x,
---y, 0, 0, -0.5, -0.5) put the top-left corner of a 400 by 400 model right of and below (x, y) by half its size.
---@param x integer Absolute horizontal coordinate to move this component to in interface units
---@param y integer Absolute vertical coordinate to move this component to in interface units
---@param parentPercentageX? number If specified, offsets this component's horizontal origin based on a percentage of its parent's width.
---@param parentPercentageY? number If specified, offsets this component's vertical origin based on a percentage of its parent's height.
---@param selfPercentageX? number If specified, offsets this component's horizontal origin based on a percentage of its width.
---@param selfPercentageY? number If specified, offsets this component's vertical origin based on a percentage of its height.
function Component:SetPos(x, y, parentPercentageX, parentPercentageY, selfPercentageX, selfPercentageY) end

---Sets the width/height for this component, optionally taking into account the parent's dimensions.
---
---Info: `SetSize` should be preferred over using SetX and SetY separately as it involves less layout operations.
---@param x integer Absolute width in interface units to resize this component to.
---@param parentPercentageX? number If specified, offsets this component's width based on a percentage of its parent's width.
function Component:SetWidth(x, parentPercentageX) end

---Sets the width/height for this component, optionally taking into account the parent's dimensions.
---
---Info: `SetSize` should be preferred over using SetX and SetY separately as it involves less layout operations.
---@param y integer Absolute height in interface units to resize this component to.
---@param parentPercentageY? number If specified, offsets this component's height based on a percentage of its parent's height.
function Component:SetHeight(y, parentPercentageY) end

---Sets the width/height for this component, optionally taking into account the parent's dimensions.
---
---Info: `SetSize` should be preferred over using SetX and SetY separately as it involves less layout operations.
---@param x integer Absolute width in interface units to resize this component to.
---@param y integer Absolute height in interface units to resize this component to.
---@param parentPercentageX? number If specified, offsets this component's width based on a percentage of its parent's width.
---@param parentPercentageY? number If specified, offsets this component's height based on a percentage of its parent's height.
function Component:SetSize(x, y, parentPercentageX, parentPercentageY) end

---Sets the target aspect ratio the component should follow, and how it should be applied. Can also be used to disable
---aspect ratio scaling.
---
---Info: Invalid width and height ratio values will be replaced with `1` when calling this function.
---@param widthRatio integer Target width aspect ratio
---@param heightRatio integer Target height aspect ratio
---@param mode ui.AspectRatioMode Indicates how the component scales based on its target aspect ratio
function Component:SetAspectRatio(widthRatio, heightRatio, mode) end

---Destroys this component, along with any other components that might have been attached to it.
---
---Note: Plugins can't delete components belonging to other plugins.
function Component:Destroy() end

---Moves this component to the front/back of the render order, causing it to draw on top/below of components that have
---the same parent.
function Component:MoveToFront() end

---Moves this component to the front/back of the render order, causing it to draw on top/below of components that have
---the same parent.
function Component:MoveToBack() end

---Triggers a layout update on this component.
---
---Info: You should generally never need to call this directly, as it is automatically called whenever a layout
---modifying operation (eg. `SetSize`) occurs on a component.
function Component:UpdateLayout() end

---Subscribes a listener for an event hook, setting a callback to be triggered whenever this event occurs, and
---optionally assigning it an ID allowing it to be referenced to in the future.
---
---Info: IDs are specific to an event hook type, the component they're attached to, and the current plugin, so the same
---ID can be used across different components or events, and doesn't need to be unique per plugin as well.
---@param hook ui.Hook The event hook to listen for.
---@param callback fun(...: any): boolean? The callback to trigger on this event, with parameters varying based on the event hook type. Can return a boolean indicating whether or not to continue processing listeners afterwards. If omitted, the callback is treated as if it returned true, resulting in other listeners still getting triggered.
---@overload fun(self: ui.Component, hook: ui.Hook, id: string, callback: fun(...: any): boolean?)
function Component:Subscribe(hook, callback) end

---Removes the listener set for the specified hook with the provided ID, or the default listener for that hook if
---omitted, from that component.
---@param hook ui.Hook The event hook to listen for.
---@overload fun(self: ui.Component, hook: ui.Hook, id: string)
function Component:Unsubscribe(hook) end

---Removes all event listeners of the specified type from this component associated with the current plugin.
---@param hook ui.Hook The event hook to clear the listeners for.
function Component:UnsubscribeAll(hook) end

---The `ui.Hook` table contains a list of all potential event hooks that can be attached to a component.
---
---These events are only triggered when using a touchscreen.
---
---Warning: Controller support is experimental and any usage of these events should be avoided.
---
---These events are associated with actions that the local player is taking in the game world.
---
---These events represent data updates received from the server which may need to be reflected on the user interface.
---@class ui.Hook
---@field ONBUTTONPRESSED ui.Hook Supported by ui.Button, ui.Check Triggered whenever the user interacts with this button/check. Non-toggle buttons will always receive `1` and `0` for current/previous values respectively. Its callbacks take self : `Component<T>`, currentValue : Int, previousValue : Int.
---@field ONCONTENTCHANGED ui.Hook Supported by ui.InputField Triggered whenever a user interacts with an input field component in a way that may affect its contents. Its callbacks take self : `Component<T>`, reason : ui.InputFieldActionResult, newContents : String.
---@field ONSELECTIONCHANGED ui.Hook Supported by ui.Carousel, ui.PagedLayer, ui.Slider `entryID` represents the component's entry that's had its selected status changed, while a `selectedStatus` of `1` indicates this entry has been selected and `0` indicates it has been deselected. Its callbacks take self : `Component<T>`, entryID : Int, selectedStatus : Int. Supported by ui.ComboField, ui.List, ui.RadioGroup `entryID` represents the component's entry that's had its selected status changed. Its callbacks take self : `Component<T>`, entryID : Int, selectionEventType : ui.SelectionChangeEvent. Supported by ui.RadialProgressOverlay Triggered whenever this radial's progress changes. `progressPc` is received as a 0..1 number representing 0 to 100%. Its callbacks take self : `Component<T>`, curValue : Float, progressPc.
---@field ONCUTSCENEFINISHED ui.Hook Supported by ui.CutsceneLayer Triggered when a cutscene finishes playing on a cutscene layer component. Its callbacks take self : `Component<T>`, reason : ui.CutscenePlaybackEndReason.
---@field ONCLICK ui.Hook Triggered when the user clicks the left mouse button or taps on this component. Its callbacks take self : `Component<T>`, x : Int, y : Int.
---@field ONCLICKREPEAT ui.Hook Triggered when the user clicks the left mouse button or taps on this component. Its callbacks take self : `Component<T>`, x : Int, y : Int.
---@field ONRELEASE ui.Hook Triggered when the user stops clicking on this component or stops a tap gesture. Its callbacks take self : `Component<T>`, x : Int, y : Int.
---@field ONHOLD ui.Hook Triggered while the user is clicking on this component. Its callbacks take self : `Component<T>`, x : Int, y : Int.
---@field ONMOUSEOVER ui.Hook Triggered when the cursor enters this component's region. Its callbacks take self : `Component<T>`, x : Int, y : Int.
---@field ONMOUSEREPEAT ui.Hook Triggered while the cursor is over this component's region. Its callbacks take self : `Component<T>`, x : Int, y : Int.
---@field ONMOUSELEAVE ui.Hook Triggered when the cursor leaves this component's region. Its callbacks take self : `Component<T>`, x : Int, y : Int.
---@field ONDRAG ui.Hook Triggered when the user starts dragging this component. Its callbacks take self : `Component<T>`, dragStartX : Int, dragStartY : Int.
---@field ONDRAGCOMPLETE ui.Hook Triggered when the user finishes dragging this component. Its callbacks take self : `Component<T>`, dragDestination : `Component<T>`, dragEndX : Int, dragEndY : Int.
---@field ONSCROLLWHEEL ui.Hook Triggered when the user moves the mouse's scrollwheel. Its callbacks take self : `Component<T>`, scrollWheelYDelta : Int.
---@field ONKEY ui.Hook Triggered when the user inputs a key on their keyboard. Its callbacks take self : `Component<T>`, keyCode : Int, keyChar : Int.
---@field ONSWIPEVERTICAL ui.Hook Triggered whenever a horizontal swipe motion occurs. Its callbacks take self : `Component<T>`, swipeCurrentX : Int, swipeCurrentY : Int.
---@field ONSWIPEHORIZONTAL ui.Hook Triggered whenever a vertical swipe motion occurs. Its callbacks take self : `Component<T>`, swipeCurrentX : Int, swipeCurrentY : Int.
---@field ONSWIPECOMPLETE ui.Hook Triggered when a swipe gesture terminates. Its callbacks take self : `Component<T>`.
---@field ONPINCHHORIZONTAL ui.Hook Triggered whenever a horizontal pinch motion occurs. Direction is `-1` for inwards pinch gestures, and 1 for outwards. Its callbacks take self : `Component<T>`, direction : Int.
---@field ONPINCHVERTICAL ui.Hook Triggered whenever a vertical pinch motion occurs. Direction is `-1` for inwards pinch gestures, and 1 for outwards. Its callbacks take self : `Component<T>`, direction : Int.
---@field ONPINCHCOMPLETE ui.Hook Triggered when a pinch gesture terminates. Its callbacks take self : `Component<T>`.
---@field ONGAMEPADBUTTON ui.Hook Its callbacks take self : `Component<T>`, buttonID : Int, buttonValue : Int.
---@field ONGAMEPADBUTTONHELD ui.Hook Its callbacks take self : `Component<T>`, buttonID : Int.
---@field ONGAMEPADAXIS ui.Hook Its callbacks take self : `Component<T>`, axisID : Int, axisValue : Int.
---@field ONGAMEPADTRIGGER ui.Hook Its callbacks take self : `Component<T>`, triggerID : Int, triggerValue : Int.
---@field ONOP ui.Hook Triggered whenever the user interacts with something in the game world, or with a UI component that has ops specified for its interactions. Its callbacks take self : `Component<T>`, opID : Int, opBaseName : String.
---@field ONOPT ui.Hook Triggered when the user selects another UI component while in target selection mode. Its callbacks take self : `Component<T>`, target : `Component<T>`.
---@field ONTARGETENTER ui.Hook Triggered when the component enters target selection mode. Its callbacks take self : `Component<T>`.
---@field ONTARGETLEAVE ui.Hook Triggered when the component leaves target selection mode. Its callbacks take self : `Component<T>`.
---@field ONVARPTRANSMIT ui.Hook Triggered when the game client receives a server transmission for player variables. Its callbacks take self : `Component<T>`.
---@field ONINVTRANSMIT ui.Hook Triggered when the game client receives a server transmission for inventories. Its callbacks take self : `Component<T>`.
---@field ONSTATTRANSMIT ui.Hook Triggered when the game client receives a server transmission for stats. Its callbacks take self : `Component<T>`.
---@field ONVARCTRANSMIT ui.Hook Triggered when the game client receives a server transmission for client variables. Its callbacks take self : `Component<T>`.
---@field ONVARCSTRTRANSMIT ui.Hook Triggered when the game client receives a server transmission for client string variables. Its callbacks take self : `Component<T>`.
---@field ONVARCLANTRANSMIT ui.Hook Triggered when the game client receives a server transmission for clan variables. Its callbacks take self : `Component<T>`.
---@field ONCHATTRANSMIT ui.Hook Triggered when the game client receives a server transmission for chat messages. Its callbacks take self : `Component<T>`.
---@field ONFRIENDTRANSMIT ui.Hook Triggered when the game client receives a server transmission for friends data. Its callbacks take self : `Component<T>`.
---@field ONCLANTRANSMIT ui.Hook Triggered when the game client receives a server transmission for clan data. Its callbacks take self : `Component<T>`.
---@field ONCLANSETTINGSTRANSMIT ui.Hook Triggered when the game client receives a server transmission for clan settings data. Its callbacks take self : `Component<T>`.
---@field ONCLANCHANNELTRANSMIT ui.Hook Triggered when the game client receives a server transmission for clan chat messages. Its callbacks take self : `Component<T>`.
---@field ONRELATIONSHIPSETTRANSMIT ui.Hook Triggered when the game client receives a server transmission for friends/clans/ignore lists. Its callbacks take self : `Component<T>`.
---@field ONMISCTRANSMIT ui.Hook Triggered when the game client receives a server transmission for miscellaneous data. Its callbacks take self : `Component<T>`.
---@field ONSTOCKTRANSMIT ui.Hook Triggered when the game client receives a server transmission for stock data. Its callbacks take self : `Component<T>`.
---@field ONPLAYERGROUPTRANSMIT ui.Hook Triggered when the game client receives a server transmission involving the current player group state. Its callbacks take self : `Component<T>`.
---@field ONPLAYERGROUPVARPTRANSMIT ui.Hook Triggered when the game client receives a server transmission for the current group's player variable. Its callbacks take self : `Component<T>`.
---@field ONCAMERAUPDATETRANSMIT ui.Hook Triggered when the game client receives a server transmission involving camera changes. Its callbacks take self : `Component<T>`.
---@field ONTIMER ui.Hook Triggered once per logic tick. Prefer using PluginLogic over this as it's a more general solution. Its callbacks take self : `Component<T>`.
---@field ONDIALOGABORT ui.Hook Triggered manually by the server. Its callbacks take self : `Component<T>`.
---@field ONSUBCHANGE ui.Hook Triggered whenever a sub-interface loads. Its callbacks take self : `Component<T>`.
---@field ONCAMFINISHED ui.Hook Triggered whenever a server-controlled camera motion finishes. Its callbacks take self : `Component<T>`.
---@field ONRESIZE ui.Hook Triggered whenever this component has its dimensions changed. Its callbacks take self : `Component<T>`.
ui.Hook = {}

---Identifies the source of a `ONSELECTIONCHANGED` event on a component's entry.
---@enum ui.SelectionChangeEvent
ui.SelectionChangeEvent = {
    ---This entry has been deselected by the user.
    DESELECTED = 0,
    ---This entry has been selected by the user.
    SELECTED = 1,
    ---This entry cannot be selected as the maximum number of entries are already selected.
    ERROR_MAX_SELECTED = 2,
    ---This entry cannot be selected as it's disabled.
    ERROR_NOT_SELECTABLE = 3,
}
